From 49df4b0f306bd036292bf29cc2e04f2c1bdedbcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gli_acopo <82150202+GliAcopo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:16:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] image_to_pdf: use Qt for raster images again

Since r14602 (bug #66706), image_to_pdf only uses Qt if
qt_supports (pdf), which is always false (qt_supports excludes pdf, ps
and eps), so raster images that Qt reads (GIF, BMP, WebP, ...) go to the
Scheme converters.  These convert the image to EPS first.  Qt5 cannot
write EPS, and ImageMagick often may not (security policy of Debian,
Ubuntu, ...): the conversion fails, but the converter still reports
success and returns an empty A4 page, so the image silently disappears
from the exported PDF.

The fix of r14602 is needed in image_to_eps, where Qt5 indeed cannot write
PostScript, but qt_image_to_pdf writes PDF files with QPrinter: drop the
condition in image_to_pdf only, as in TeXmacs 2.1.4.
---
 src/System/Files/image_files.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/System/Files/image_files.cpp b/src/System/Files/image_files.cpp
index 236d4ead4..fe29a1d76 100644
--- a/src/System/Files/image_files.cpp
+++ b/src/System/Files/image_files.cpp
@@ -504,7 +504,8 @@ image_to_pdf (url image, url pdf, int w_pt, int h_pt, int dpi) {
 #endif
   //converters below will yield only raster images.
 #ifdef QTTEXMACS
-  if (qt_supports (image) && qt_supports (pdf)) {
+  // not qt_supports (pdf), which is always false: Qt writes PDF files
+  if (qt_supports (image)) {
     if (DEBUG_CONVERT) debug_convert << " using qt "<<LF;
     qt_image_to_pdf (image, pdf, w_pt, h_pt, dpi);
     return;
-- 
2.53.0

